<div id="pf69" class="pf w0 h0" data-page-no="69"><div class="pc pc69 w0 h0"><img class="bi x0 y0 w1 h1" alt="" src="data:image/png;base64,"/><div class="c x1 y65 w2 hb"><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y966 ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data architecture</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y967 ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Software engineering</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y968 ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Orchestration</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y969 ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">A data engineer has several top-level goals across the data lifecycle—</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y96a ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">produce optimum ROI and reduce costs (financial and opportunity), reduce</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y96b ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">risk (security<span class="_ _2"></span>, data quality) and maximize data value and utility<span class="_ _2"></span>. In the next</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y96c ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">chapter<span class="_ _0"></span>, we’ll discuss how these elements impact the design of good</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y96d ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">architecture. Subsequently<span class="_ _2"></span>, we’ve devoted a chapter to each of the stages of</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y96e ffd fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">the data engineering lifecycle.</div><div class="t m0 x2f hd y96f ff10 fs3 fc2 sc0 ls0 ws0">1<span class="_ _a"> </span><span class="ffd fc0"> Evren Eryurek, Uri Gilad, V<span class="_ _b"></span>alliappa Lakshmanan, Anita Kibunguchy-Grant, and Jessi</span></div><div class="t m0 x30 h10 y970 ffd fs3 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Ashdown,<span class="ffe"> Data Governance: The Definitive Guide </span>(O’Reilly),</div><div class="t m0 x30 h10 y971 ffd fs3 fc2 sc0 ls0 ws0">https://learning.oreilly<span class="_ _2"></span>.com/library/view/data-governance-the/9781492063483/<span class="fc0">.</span></div><div class="t m0 x2f hd y972 ff10 fs3 fc2 sc0 ls0 ws0">2<span class="_ _a"> </span><span class="ffd fc0"> Eryurek et al.</span></div><div class="t m0 x2f hd y973 ff10 fs3 fc2 sc0 ls0 ws0">3<sp